1.3.3 Enumerate the CrushFTP Web Application:
The application is a file transfer solution with a login page for user authentication. No default usernames or passwords are provided, which may reduce unauthorized access risks. Recommendations include investigating the login page for vulnerabilities, testing for SQL Injection, XSS, CSRF, and reviewing configuration settings for security best practices.}
   1.4 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.3.4 Summary of Vulnerabilities in CrushFTP:
Notable vulnerabilities include CVE-2025-31161 (Authentication Bypass), CVE-2024-4040 (VFS Sandbox Escape), and CVE-2025-54309 (AS2 Validation Flaw). Recommendations include prompt patching, vulnerability monitoring, and implementing security best practices.}
   1.4 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.3.5 Summary of CVE-2024-4040 Exploitation Findings:
Successfully exploited CVE-2024-4040 leading to unauthorized access to `/etc/passwd`, retrieval of session tokens, and identification of sensitive user data. Recommendations include investigating further vulnerabilities, reviewing access controls, and considering patching.}
   1.4 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.3.6 Summary of Extracted User Data from CrushFTP:
Successfully extracted `/var/opt/CrushFTP10/users/MainUsers/deathflash/user.XML`, which contains sensitive information including an MD5 hashed password. Recommendations include investigating the feasibility of cracking the MD5 hash, reviewing access control settings, and implementing stronger password hashing mechanisms.}
   1.4 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.3.7 Summary of Password Disclosure for User "deathflash":
The password for the user account "deathflash" has been successfully extracted and is easily guessable, indicating a potential security weakness. Recommendations include changing the password to a strong, complex one, enforcing a robust password policy, educating users on password security, reviewing access logs for unauthorized attempts, and implementing multi-factor authentication.}
   1.4 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.4 Summary of Active Session Findings:
Successful login achieved, establishing an active session. Despite having an active session, no additional valuable information or sensitive data has been located. Recommendations include continuing to explore the application’s functionalities, investigating for administrative privileges, checking for access to sensitive user data or configuration files, conducting a thorough vulnerability assessment for XSS, CSRF, IDOR, and reviewing session management practices.}
   1.5 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.5 Summary of Vulnerabilities in CrushFTP:
CrushFTP has critical vulnerabilities including CVE-2025-54309 (Zero-Day, Exploited in the Wild), CVE-2025-2825 / CVE-2025-31161 (Authentication Bypass, Exploited in the Wild), CVE-2023-43177 (Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution), and CVE-2024-4040 (VFS Sandbox Escape / Server-Side Template Injection, Exploited in the Wild). Recommendations include immediate updates to the latest stable versions, implementing DMZ proxy, monitoring for compromise, and network segmentation.}  
   1.6 Target IP - 10.129.231.140

1.6 Summary of Successful Exploitation of CVE-2023-43177:
Successfully exploited CVE-2023-43177, gaining root access through unauthenticated remote code execution, indicating complete control over the target system. Recommendations include patching the vulnerability immediately, conducting a system audit, reviewing access controls, implementing monitoring solutions, developing an incident response plan, and providing training on timely patch management.}  
   1.7 Target IP - 10.129.231.140
